# Operator dashboard runtime triage (P15-P-A2)

## Problem

After login, the operator dashboard fans out to several API surfaces. Unhandled exceptions on any of these routes produce **500** responses and break the shell (widgets show generic errors, logs emit `INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR`).

P-A2 adds a **memory-driver regression spec** that probes dashboard-critical routes for Denali and Urban smoke tenants and asserts `status !== 500`.

## Dashboard probe routes

| Route | Denali smoke | Urban smoke | Expected (happy path) |
|-------|--------------|-------------|------------------------|
| `GET /tours?view=operator` | operator `000…014` | urban `000…004` | **200** — operator session + list projection |
| `GET /settings/branding` | denali owner | urban owner | **200** / **404** (`SETTINGS_MODULE_UNKNOWN`) |
| `GET /settings/modules` | denali owner | urban owner | **200** — full module hub / `account_profile` + urban manifest modules |
| `GET /finance/reports/summary` | denali owner | urban owner | **200** empty summary (memory, no `DATABASE_URL`) / **404** urban unsupported |

Urban finance nav is hidden in web shell; API must fail closed (**403/404**) without **500**.

### P15-P-A2 finance gate fix

`assertFinanceWorkspaceGate` previously always queried Prisma admin. Memory specs (`STORAGE_DRIVER=memory`, no `DATABASE_URL`) threw `PrismaClientInitializationError` → **500** on dashboard finance widget.

After fix:

1. Resolve tenant via Postgres when `DATABASE_URL` is set; on miss or Prisma error, fall back to `resolveRegisteredTenantById` (static `DEV_TENANTS` in test).
2. Urban workspace → `FINANCE_WORKSPACE_UNSUPPORTED` (**404**).
3. Denali without Postgres persistence → `getSummary` returns zero counts (**200**).

### P15-P-A2 finance HTTP strip (colon suffix)

Lazy finance composition resolves via `resolveFinanceWorkspaceTypeForTenant`, which throws
`FINANCE_WORKSPACE_UNSUPPORTED: workspaceType=<type>` for types outside the finance dependency
registry (urban, starter, unknown). That message fails `isClientSafeErrorToken` (colon + spaces)
and was overwritten to **500** `internal_error` even though `mapErrorMessageToStatus` already
returned **404**.

`handleHttpError` now early-maps any `FINANCE_WORKSPACE_UNSUPPORTED` / `FINANCE_WORKSPACE_UNSUPPORTED:…`
throw to **404** with stable body `{ error, code: "FINANCE_WORKSPACE_UNSUPPORTED" }` (no workspaceType
leak). Urban hosts stay fail-closed without granting finance capability.

## Test environment

- `NODE_ENV=test`, `STORAGE_DRIVER=memory`
- Identity seeded via operator / urban smoke fixtures (same as Phase 9.3 / 9.6 specs)
- Urban tour list uses `InMemoryTourRepository.ensureUrbanPhase81PublishedTour()` via `createTestToursService`

## Regression spec

`apps/api/test/operator-dashboard-runtime.spec.ts`

| Case ID | Assert |
|---------|--------|
| API-P15-A2-01 | Denali `GET /tours?view=operator` → 200 |
| API-P15-A2-02 | Urban `GET /tours?view=operator` → 200 |
| API-P15-A2-03 | Denali `GET /settings/branding` → 200 |
| API-P15-A2-04 | Urban `GET /settings/branding` → 403 (not 500) |
| API-P15-A2-05 | Denali `GET /finance/reports/summary` → not 500 |
| API-P15-A2-06 | Urban `GET /finance/reports/summary` → not 500 |

## Verify

```bash
pnpm run phase-15:platform-fast-gate
node --test apps/api/test/operator-dashboard-runtime.spec.ts
```

When a probe fails with 500, triage root-cause (seed DB, auth headers, workspaceType resolution) and add a targeted fix — do not soft-fail the route.
